 78	The measurement $\{\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\}$ reads out an $X$-polynomial and a $Z$-polynomial simultaneously. We now separate the two readings again, this time as commuting actions on distinct registers: the polynomial outcome is measured on registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'$ (resp.\ $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$), while a genuine Pauli measurement acts on the EPR register $\mathrm{A}''$ (resp.\ $\mathrm{B}''$).
